              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "обычай (obýchay) — \"a custom\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "По русскому обычаю гостей встречают хлебом и солью. Po rússkomu obýchayu gostéy vstrecháyut khlébom i sólyu. By Russian custom, guests are welcomed with bread and salt."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Masculine."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "обычай (obýchay) is inherited from Proto-Slavic obvyčajĭ (EtymDB), built on vyknǫti \"to get used to\", the root of привыкать."
            }
          ]
        },
